# Copy to settings.env, fill these four values, then run python3 configure.py.
# This file is data, not a shell script. Keep it private (chmod 600 settings.env).
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
CALLIOPE_ADMIN_EMAIL=
CALLIOPE_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
CALLIOPE_PUBLIC_URL=https://calliope.example.com

# Use the browser-facing LAN/public address above when connecting from elsewhere.
# For automatic HTTPS use a real DNS hostname and expose ports 80 and 443.
# Replace calliope.example.com with this server's name. Calliope and /mcp share HTTPS.
# Remote addresses, including LAN addresses, require HTTPS for MCP OAuth.
# Plain HTTP is supported only on localhost for development.
# DataRabbit is enabled at https://YOUR_SERVER_NAME:3001 using the same login
# and certificate. Allow TCP 3001 through the host/cloud firewall as well.
# Optional: choose another port on that SAME hostname (no extra DNS required).
# CALLIOPE_DATA_URL=https://calliope.example.com:3001
# CALLIOPE_DATA_BIND=3001
# For development on localhost, the DataRabbit listener stays loopback-only.
# Optional ACME contact (separate from the Calliope account; blank is valid):
# CALLIOPE_ACME_EMAIL=operator@example.com
# PostgreSQL is also published; SQL uses its own TLS protocol on port 5432.
# CALLIOPE_SQL_HOST=calliope.example.com
# CALLIOPE_SQL_BIND=0.0.0.0:5432
# Or bind only the server's LAN address, for example 192.168.1.20:5432.
# Generated SQL certificates: copy state/postgres-tls/ca.crt to remote clients.
# To use your own certificate chain/key, set provided and place server.crt/server.key
# in state/postgres-tls/ after configure.py and before docker compose up.
# CALLIOPE_SQL_TLS=generated
# Behind your own HTTPS reverse proxy (Caddy, nginx, Traefik), for example a LAN
# name with an internal certificate: the proxy serves CALLIOPE_PUBLIC_URL and
# CALLIOPE_DATA_URL and forwards to these plain listeners. Name the address the
# proxy connects from; only it may set X-Forwarded-Proto/Host.
# CALLIOPE_TLS=proxy
# CALLIOPE_TRUSTED_PROXIES=192.168.1.10
# CALLIOPE_HTTP_BIND=127.0.0.1:8080
# CALLIOPE_DATA_BIND=127.0.0.1:8081
# Optional persistent CPU desktop (no GPU required):
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=computer
# COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=calliope
# Callie's long-term memory is shared across every conversation, so what she worked
# out with one person helps the next. To recall only what everyone in a conversation
# could see (people, Teams, or everyone it is shared with), set:
# CALLIOPE_MEMORY_SCOPE=audience
# Callie writes what people tell her as quoted claims (who said it, word for word).
# To go back to Hindsight's own extraction, set:
# CALLIOPE_MEMORY_EXTRACTOR=hindsight
